(* Quest Self-Hosted Compiler: The SSA's Trampolines Interface
 *
 * Makes an export its function (docs/ssa.md section 4.1). Another unit calls
 * a module's function through its export, qv_, which passes the function's
 * environment as null and tail-calls it, often through an adapter of the
 * unit's own (ir.md section 8.4.1) that tail-calls the function in turn:
 * vector.get was three branches, where the C build's export is the function,
 * since clang inlines the two. An exported function of one block that ends in
 * a tail call of a function of the unit gets a copy of that function in place
 * of the call, again while that block still ends in such a call, up to 4
 * times, so that an adapter is copied in and then the function it calls. A
 * function is copied when it has at most 64 instructions, every call it makes
 * is a tail call or one in a block that never ends (a raise), it takes the
 * call's arguments as they are passed, its results are the export's, and
 * tailJumps.copiable says it can be. Its other callers are left as they
 * are. *)

interface Trampolines
import
    ssa = questlang/ssa/nodes : questlang/ssa/Nodes
export
    trampolineUnit(u: ssa.Unit): Ok
end
